From 0a4c9b55da6a86de35ffc1fee51219ea494bfd66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:10:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 112/119] gpu/vulkan: Mali fallbacks, failure reasons and GPU
 emulation (from DS2)

- rex_vulkan_failure_reason: '<GPU>: <reason>' for every device rejection and a failed SetupContext.
- Android no longer requires geometryShader or fillModeNonSolid (fallbacks exist);
  vulkan_require_vertex_pipeline_stores_and_atomics is a real cvar (still on): off, vertex
  memexport draws are left out and counted per shader hash.
- Stored pipelines needing clip/cull distances the device lacks are skipped.
- vulkan_emulate_gpu=mali|mali_vk11|panvk (+ _keep) hides features on a full GPU.
- 8-bit gamma render targets without R16G16B16A16_UNORM and interlock.
- clamp_depth vertex modification bit (modification bit 38) without depthClamp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

